      "title": "Tata Sons board members to visit Air India HQ, review performance on Nov 19",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/companies/news/tata-sons-board-members-to-visit-air-india-hq-review-performance-on-nov-19-126111801439_1.html",
      "description": "Tata Sons board members, including Chairman N Chandrasekaran and Noel Tata, will be visiting Air India headquarters in Gurugram on Thursday, according to sources.\nAir India is co-owned by Tata Sons and Singapore Airlines, which holds a 25.1 per cent stake.\nThe sources said the members will be reviewing the performance of the loss-making Air India. The airline's MD and CEO Tewolde Gebremariam will be making a presentation to the members, they added.\nBesides, operational integration of Air India and Air India Express is likely to be discussed, the sources said.\nTata Sons Chairman Chandrasekaran, board member Noel Tata and others will be visiting the Air India headquarters on Thursday, they added.\nIt could not be immediately ascertained whether all the Tata Sons board members will be visiting the airline's headquarters.\nOther members on the Tata Sons board are Venu Srinivasan, Harish Manwani, Anita Marangoly George and Saurabh Agrawal.\nThere was no comment from Air India on the pla",
